{"data": [{"author_id": "1499097979747291138", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:10:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116639073787912195"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/SmallCapSnipa/…", "end": 220, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/SmallCapSnipa/status/2116542959264969033", "start": 197, "url": "https://t.co/kfFkZZ1irc"}]}, "id": "2116639073787912195", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116542959264969033", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The Nscale one doesn't surprise me. Ran the numbers on a UK compute project last year, industrial power at $0.25 to $0.35/kWh makes most GPU cluster economics fall over before you've hired anyone. https://t.co/kfFkZZ1irc", "url": "https://x.com/chessieowl/status/2116639073787912195"}, {"author_id": "2110111835433082880", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:55:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116650168191959207"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/9Xm0MPMKin", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/UseOffPeak/status/2116650168191959207/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116288036522663936", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/9Xm0MPMKin"}]}, "id": "2116650168191959207", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 44, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "52.3% average GPU use. Easy to read as half a cluster sitting free.\n\nThe Philly trace (Microsoft, ATC 2019) measured activity on GPUs already allocated. Available supply is a separate check.\n\nPublished research, not Offpeak results. That's why spare GPUs are worth testing. https://t.co/9Xm0MPMKin", "url": "https://x.com/UseOffPeak/status/2116650168191959207"}, {"author_id": "1291510399116902402", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:36:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116645386794275077"], "id": "2116645386794275077", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 92, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A single B200 is now mining on KubeTEE (SN90), running confidential workloads inside a TEE (a locked part of the chip that proves what code ran).\n\nThat's the product: the subnet scores attested capacity, not tokens. A cluster proves it can schedule confidential GPU jobs, and a", "url": "https://x.com/taoleeh/status/2116645386794275077"}, {"author_id": "1908700448388730881", "created_at": "2026-10-31T23:16:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116670559534600261"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/xrxomhqylU", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/hineycoin/status/2116670559534600261/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116670556825165824", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/xrxomhqylU"}]}, "id": "2116670559534600261", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 195, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What people actually use Akash Network for:\n\n🧠 GPU compute for AI training and inference\n🌐 Hosting websites and Docker apps\n🤖 AkashML, hosted open models through an OpenAI-compatible API\n🏠 Homenode, beta sign-ups for home GPU owners\n\nA cloud for builders who want open access. https://t.co/xrxomhqylU", "url": "https://x.com/hineycoin/status/2116670559534600261"}, {"author_id": "1797337858140753920", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:56:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116650611286712473"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 163, "start": 159, "tag": "NRV"}, {"end": 168, "start": 164, "tag": "SUI"}, {"end": 173, "start": 169, "tag": "SOL"}]}, "id": "2116650611286712473", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Let's dive into the world of decentralized worker nodes! These nodes harness green GPU compute and hardware to securely power AI training on Sui &amp; Solana. $NRV $SUI $SOL", "url": "https://x.com/KrasaLuxury/status/2116650611286712473"}, {"author_id": "184144812", "created_at": "2026-10-31T22:20:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116656694692356127"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JCc0O7DDGs", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Gatman180/status/2116656694692356127/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116656687218044928", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/JCc0O7DDGs"}]}, "id": "2116656694692356127", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 274, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "🇬🇲🇬🇲: The Gambia Press Union (GPU) trained over 100 journalists in election reporting and safety ahead of the December 5 presidential election. The training, conducted in collaboration with Reporters Without Borders and supported by the Canada Fund for Local Initiatives, covered https://t.co/JCc0O7DDGs", "url": "https://x.com/Gatman180/status/2116656694692356127"}, {"author_id": "361519062", "created_at": "2026-10-31T22:30:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116659125820002606"], "id": "2116659125820002606", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Using Luna to automated multiple ASL Machine Learning training, just realized it was not using my GPU.  Got it fixed and wow much faster.  :0)\n\nLuna is great at some things but miss over bigger pictures like larger models.", "url": "https://x.com/RustyOnLife/status/2116659125820002606"}, {"author_id": "1724095664240709633", "created_at": "2026-10-31T22:09:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116653763658494421"], "id": "2116653763658494421", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Musk on Colossus 2: three clusters get 220k GB300s each, wired for training. Spam gets ~200k GB300s for inference, with much simpler networking and less than half the fiber.\n\nSame chip, half the fiber. As the mix tilts to inference, networking per GPU is the line that shrinks.", "url": "https://x.com/bqq_carry/status/2116653763658494421"}, {"author_id": "1299699294", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:48:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116648619319136701"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/elonmusk/statu…", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/2116596535433871630", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/ebvVUV3rMb"}]}, "id": "2116648619319136701", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116596535433871630", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Elon Musk says Colossus 2 in Memphis is targeting roughly 1.2 MILLION NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs by year-end.\n\nThe campus breakdown:\n\n• Macrohard: 110K GB200s + 220K GB300s\n• Macroharder: 220K GB300s for training\n• Minihard: 220K GB300s for training, operational since October\n• https://t.co/ebvVUV3rMb", "url": "https://x.com/SatyaOnMarkets/status/2116648619319136701"}, {"author_id": "1469759292798603266", "created_at": "2026-10-31T23:21:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116671909106491757"], "id": "2116671909106491757", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 105, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "NVIDIA Brev users were reportedly notified that their SSH keys may have been exposed 🫠\n\nThis could give attackers access to GPU instances running sensitive AI workloads, including models, training data, and credentials.\n\nWe wrote a quick breakdown of what happened, the risks,", "url": "https://x.com/YakirKad/status/2116671909106491757"}, {"author_id": "1977011373805830144", "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:42:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116646989391929474"], "id": "2116646989391929474", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, 